      "message": "nit: `process_console_output_line()` uses `regex.match(line_str)` (which anchors at the start of the string and relies on the leading `.*` in `SINGLE_CHECK_FAILED_REGEX`), whereas `self.assertRegex()` uses `regex.search()`. Also, `TEST_ASSERT` in `include/test_util.h` prefixes `ASSERTION failed:` with `%s:%d: ` (e.g., `\"test/foo.c:42: ASSERTION failed: x \u003d\u003d y\"`).\n\nIf the leading `.*` were ever accidentally removed from `SINGLE_CHECK_FAILED_REGEX`, `self.assertRegex()` would still pass while `regex.match()` in `process_console_output_line()` would fail to match lines with prefixes. Consider testing `SINGLE_CHECK_FAILED_REGEX.match(...)` (or `process_console_output_line()` directly) and including a prefix like `\"test/foo.c:42: \"` on the `ASSERTION failed:` test string.",
